  "details": "Please add 16Bit floats to Global Avatar Parameters, both unsynced and synced (the usual checkbox).\n\nThese will obviously take 16 memory instead of 8.\n\nSome of us would use more than 256 values onto one parameter.\n\nIt is required for a uses that need high precision.\n\nWhat happens with the standard float that is used, is that it will act as a 32bit float, but over the network it is synced as a 8bit minifloat, which can produce difference results for local and remote clients.",
